<title>INDIA: India soybean firm,but soyoil eases as trucks deli.</title>
<headline>India soybean firm,but soyoil eases as trucks deli.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>ver</p>
<p>Soybean prices firmed in central Indian markets on good demand from processing plants against poor arrivals. Soybean prices rose by 100-150 rupees per tonne today. The undertone was strong, traders said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices eased in light trade as truckers ended a 10-day strike and deliveries restarted. Traders said the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on very limited supply from Indian processors and exporters. Soymeal yellow was $320 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $120 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 4,200 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business was dull and the undertone was strong.</p>
